pcbkit 2

// TEENSY41 (PJRC): Teensy 4.1 (NXP i.MX RT1062 Cortex-M7 600 MHz, 1 MB RAM, 8 MB flash, PSRAM
// pads, microSD) on two 24-pin female headers 0.6" apart; pins named as its card (D0-D41, VIN,
// 3V3, GND)
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/TEENSY_41.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet: https://www.pjrc.com/store/teensy41.html (PJRC Teensy 4.1 product page and pinout
// card card11a_rev4 (front): outer pins, VIN 3.6-5.5 V, 3.3 V out 250 mA max)
// Pins: PJRC Teensy 4.1 pinout card card11a_rev4_web.pdf (front): bottom row from USB
// GND,0..12,3.3V,24..32; top row from USB Vin,GND,3.3V,23..13,GND,41..33
// Footprint: as given
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: VIN and VUSB are joined on the Teensy: cut the VUSB-VIN pads on its bottom before powering
// VIN while USB is plugged, or feed VIN through a diode/ideal-diode as here.
// Note: Programming: the separate MKL02 bootloader chip (HalfKay) loads a .hex over USB with
// Teensy Loader / teensy_loader_cli; the program button forces it.
// Note: The microSD socket (4-bit SDIO, BUILTIN_SDCARD) and the two QSPI PSRAM pads (APS6404L, 8
// MB each; FlexSPI2) are on the module itself.

/// TEENSY41 — Teensy 4.1 (NXP i.MX RT1062 Cortex-M7 600 MHz, 1 MB RAM, 8 MB flash, PSRAM pads,
/// microSD) on two 24-pin female headers 0.6" apart; pins named as its card (D0-D41, VIN, 3V3, GND)
part Part = device(
  footprint = moduleSocket(
